== block 9: Remark 6.6 (a chain needs as many batches as it has links)
  strings of l bits; batches of b questions fixed before the answers of the batch; s batches.
  strategy G: every batch asks the known list (which reveals the next string) and b-1 lists
  'known list + a guess of the next string + a guess of the one after', guesses never repeated.
  A batch reveals two strings instead of one exactly if one of its guesses of the next string is right;
  Pr[some batch among s does] against the bound s b/(2^l - s b):
    l = 4, b = 3, s = 2: exact 0.2344; simulated 0.2364; bound 0.6000
    l = 5, b = 4, s = 3: exact 0.2557; simulated 0.2562; bound 0.6000
    l = 6, b = 4, s = 6: exact 0.2503; simulated 0.2493; bound 0.6000
    l = 8, b = 8, s = 8: exact 0.1989; simulated 0.1981; bound 0.3333

